IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `ccc-core`

-- ccc2-treason.l4 -- Criminal Code (Canada), R.S.C., 1985, c. C-46, PART II (Offences Against Public Order), ss 46 to 48:
-- high treason, treason, their punishment, the corroboration rule and the limitation periods. Layer 1 (the law, objectively).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering, made by a converter script, of the Justice Laws Website consolidation (current to 2026-09-30).
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here is claimed verified against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER (the rule of 2026-10-29, assumed, not ruled by a lawyer; see NOTES.md "Reading a result: FALSE and NOTHING (ccc2)").
--   JUST TRUE   the facts bring the case within the provision on the text's own words.
--   JUST FALSE  the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition; a condition introduced with "if", "unless", "where", "until";
--               a flat negative "no person shall", "is not admissible"; a period the text fixes in its own words).
--   NOTHING     not covered: an offence-creating "Every one who ..." clause whose element is unmet (the text lists the conduct, it does not say no to
--               other conduct), a case outside a limit the text sets in its own words ("in Canada"), a list not closed, a borrowed term.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE. Every branch that answers JUST FALSE carries a FALSE-kind tag quoting the text's own words
-- and every branch that answers NOTHING carries a NOTHING-kind tag giving its reason.
-- Every top-level name and every constructor begins with the label of the provision it implements (s 46(1), s 47(2) ...).

§ `Section 46 -- High treason`

-- src:854 | 46 (1) Every one commits high treason who, in Canada,
-- src:855 | (a) kills or attempts to kill Her Majesty, or does her any bodily harm tending to death or destruction, maims or wounds her, or imprisons or restrains her;
-- src:856 | (b) levies war against Canada or does any act preparatory thereto; or
-- src:857 | (c) assists an enemy at war with Canada, or any armed forces against whom Canadian Forces are engaged in hostilities, whether or not a state of war exists between Canada and the country whose forces they are.
@ref Criminal Code s 46(1) (high treason) (src:854-857)
DECLARE `s 46(1) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 46(1)(a) kills or attempts to kill Her Majesty`
    `s 46(1)(a) does Her Majesty any bodily harm tending to death or destruction`
    `s 46(1)(a) maims or wounds Her Majesty`
    `s 46(1)(a) imprisons or restrains Her Majesty`
    `s 46(1)(b) levies war against Canada`
    `s 46(1)(b) does an act preparatory to levying war against Canada`
    `s 46(1)(c) assists an enemy at war with Canada`
    `s 46(1)(c) assists armed forces against whom Canadian Forces are engaged in hostilities`
    `s 46(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)`

-- "Every one commits high treason who, in Canada, (a) ... (b) ... (c) ...": an offence-creating clause, so an unmet element is NOT the text's no (NOTHING).
@ref Criminal Code s 46(1) (high treason) (src:854-857)
GIVEN act IS A `s 46(1) act`
      `the act is done in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(1) high treason is committed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF act EQUALS `s 46(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one commits high treason who, in Canada,"
        IF `the act is done in Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in Canada"

-- Subsection (3)(a): a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada commits it while in or out of Canada, "notwithstanding subsection (1)".
-- src:865 | Canadian citizen
-- src:866 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (1) or (2), a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada,
-- src:867 | (a) commits high treason if, while in or out of Canada, he does anything mentioned in subsection (1); or
@ref Criminal Code s 46(3)(a) (Canadian citizen, high treason) (src:865-867)
GIVEN act IS A `s 46(1) act`
      `the person is a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(3)(a) the citizen or person owing allegiance commits high treason in or out of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF act EQUALS `s 46(1) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (c)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "does anything mentioned in subsection (1)"
        IF `the person is a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada"

-- src:854 | 46 (1) Every one commits high treason who, in Canada,
-- src:855 | (a) kills or attempts to kill Her Majesty, or does her any bodily harm tending to death or destruction, maims or wounds her, or imprisons or restrains her;
-- src:856 | (b) levies war against Canada or does any act preparatory thereto; or
-- src:857 | (c) assists an enemy at war with Canada, or any armed forces against whom Canadian Forces are engaged in hostilities, whether or not a state of war exists between Canada and the country whose forces they are.
-- src:865 | Canadian citizen
-- src:866 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (1) or (2), a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada,
-- src:867 | (a) commits high treason if, while in or out of Canada, he does anything mentioned in subsection (1); or
@ref Criminal Code s 46(1) and (3)(a) (high treason, in or out of Canada) (src:854-867)
GIVEN act IS A `s 46(1) act`
      `the act is done in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(1) or (3)(a) high treason is committed` MEANS
    IF `s 46(1) high treason is committed` act `the act is done in Canada` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `s 46(3)(a) the citizen or person owing allegiance commits high treason in or out of Canada` act `the person is a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): neither "in Canada" (subsection (1)) nor "a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance" (subsection (3)(a)) is met

§ `Section 46 -- Treason`

-- src:858 | Treason
-- src:859 | (2) Every one commits treason who, in Canada,
-- src:860 | (a) uses force or violence for the purpose of overthrowing the government of Canada or a province;
-- src:861 | (b) without lawful authority, communicates or makes available to an agent of a state other than Canada, military or scientific information or any sketch, plan, model, article, note or document of a military or scientific character that he knows or ought to know may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada;
-- src:862 | (c) conspires with any person to commit high treason or to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a);
-- src:863 | (d) forms an intention to do anything that is high treason or that is mentioned in paragraph (a) and manifests that intention by an overt act; or
-- src:864 | (e) conspires with any person to do anything mentioned in paragraph (b) or forms an intention to do anything mentioned in paragraph (b) and manifests that intention by an overt act.
@ref Criminal Code s 46(2) (treason) (src:858-864)
DECLARE `s 46(2) act` IS ONE OF
    `s 46(2)(a) uses force or violence for the purpose of overthrowing the government of Canada or a province`
    `s 46(2)(b) communicates or makes available military or scientific information to an agent of a state other than Canada`
    `s 46(2)(c) conspires with any person to commit high treason or to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a)`
    `s 46(2)(d) forms an intention to do high treason or anything mentioned in paragraph (a) and manifests that intention by an overt act`
    `s 46(2)(e) conspires with any person to do anything mentioned in paragraph (b)`
    `s 46(2)(e) forms an intention to do anything mentioned in paragraph (b) and manifests that intention by an overt act`
    `s 46(2) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (e)`

-- The elements each paragraph names, beyond the act itself: (b) and (e) "without lawful authority" and "that he knows or ought to know may be used by that state for a purpose
-- prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada"; (d) and the second limb of (e) "manifests that intention by an overt act".
@ref Criminal Code s 46(2) (treason) (src:858-864)
GIVEN act IS A `s 46(2) act`
      `the person acts without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows or ought to know that the information may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person manifests the intention by an overt act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 46(2) the act and its elements are those of one of paragraphs (a) to (e)` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 46(2)(a) uses force or violence for the purpose of overthrowing the government of Canada or a province` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 46(2)(b) communicates or makes available military or scientific information to an agent of a state other than Canada` THEN `the person acts without lawful authority` AND `the person knows or ought to know that the information may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada`
    WHEN `s 46(2)(c) conspires with any person to commit high treason or to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `s 46(2)(d) forms an intention to do high treason or anything mentioned in paragraph (a) and manifests that intention by an overt act` THEN `the person manifests the intention by an overt act`
    WHEN `s 46(2)(e) conspires with any person to do anything mentioned in paragraph (b)` THEN `the person acts without lawful authority` AND `the person knows or ought to know that the information may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada`
    WHEN `s 46(2)(e) forms an intention to do anything mentioned in paragraph (b) and manifests that intention by an overt act` THEN `the person acts without lawful authority` AND `the person knows or ought to know that the information may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada` AND `the person manifests the intention by an overt act`
    WHEN `s 46(2) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (e)` THEN FALSE

@ref Criminal Code s 46(2) (treason) (src:858-864)
GIVEN act IS A `s 46(2) act`
      `the act is done in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows or ought to know that the information may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person manifests the intention by an overt act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(2) treason is committed` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 46(2) the act and its elements are those of one of paragraphs (a) to (e)` act `the person acts without lawful authority` `the person knows or ought to know that the information may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada` `the person manifests the intention by an overt act`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "Every one commits treason who, in Canada,"
        IF `the act is done in Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in Canada"

-- src:865 | Canadian citizen
-- src:866 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (1) or (2), a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada,
-- src:867 | (a) commits high treason if, while in or out of Canada, he does anything mentioned in subsection (1); or
-- src:868 | (b) commits treason if, while in or out of Canada, he does anything mentioned in subsection (2).
@ref Criminal Code s 46(3)(b) (Canadian citizen, treason) (src:865-868)
GIVEN act IS A `s 46(2) act`
      `the person is a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows or ought to know that the information may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person manifests the intention by an overt act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(3)(b) the citizen or person owing allegiance commits treason in or out of Canada` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `s 46(2) the act and its elements are those of one of paragraphs (a) to (e)` act `the person acts without lawful authority` `the person knows or ought to know that the information may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada` `the person manifests the intention by an overt act`
            THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "does anything mentioned in subsection (2)"
        IF `the person is a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada"

-- src:858 | Treason
-- src:859 | (2) Every one commits treason who, in Canada,
-- src:860 | (a) uses force or violence for the purpose of overthrowing the government of Canada or a province;
-- src:861 | (b) without lawful authority, communicates or makes available to an agent of a state other than Canada, military or scientific information or any sketch, plan, model, article, note or document of a military or scientific character that he knows or ought to know may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada;
-- src:862 | (c) conspires with any person to commit high treason or to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a);
-- src:863 | (d) forms an intention to do anything that is high treason or that is mentioned in paragraph (a) and manifests that intention by an overt act; or
