-- src:865 | Canadian citizen
-- src:866 | (3) Notwithstanding subsection (1) or (2), a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada,
-- src:867 | (a) commits high treason if, while in or out of Canada, he does anything mentioned in subsection (1); or
-- src:868 | (b) commits treason if, while in or out of Canada, he does anything mentioned in subsection (2).
@ref Criminal Code s 46(2) and (3)(b) (treason, in or out of Canada) (src:858-868)
GIVEN act IS A `s 46(2) act`
      `the act is done in Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person acts without lawful authority` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person knows or ought to know that the information may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person manifests the intention by an overt act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(2) or (3)(b) treason is committed` MEANS
    IF `s 46(2) treason is committed` act `the act is done in Canada` `the person acts without lawful authority` `the person knows or ought to know that the information may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada` `the person manifests the intention by an overt act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        OR `s 46(3)(b) the citizen or person owing allegiance commits treason in or out of Canada` act `the person is a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance to Her Majesty in right of Canada` `the person acts without lawful authority` `the person knows or ought to know that the information may be used by that state for a purpose prejudicial to the safety or defence of Canada` `the person manifests the intention by an overt act` EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): neither "in Canada" (subsection (2)) nor "a Canadian citizen or a person who owes allegiance" (subsection (3)(b)) is met

-- src:869 | Overt act
-- src:870 | (4) Where it is treason to conspire with any person, the act of conspiring is an overt act of treason.
@ref Criminal Code s 46(4) (overt act) (src:869-870)
GIVEN `it is treason to conspire with the person` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46(4) the act of conspiring is an overt act of treason` MEANS
    IF `it is treason to conspire with the person` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where it is treason to conspire with any person"

§ `Section 47 -- Punishment, corroboration, minimum punishment`

-- src:871 | Punishment for high treason
-- src:872 | 47 (1) Every one who commits high treason is guilty of an indictable offence and shall be sentenced to imprisonment for life.
@ref Criminal Code s 47(1) (punishment for high treason) (src:871-872)
`s 47(1) the class of the offence of high treason` MEANS `an indictable offence`

@ref Criminal Code s 47(1) (punishment for high treason) (src:871-872)
--                                       mode           maximum imprisonment    minimum imprisonment    max fine           min fine
`s 47(1) the punishment for high treason` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `imprisonment for life`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`   -- the minimum is life by subsection (4)

-- src:873 | Punishment for treason
-- src:874 | (2) Every one who commits treason is guilty of an indictable offence and liable
-- src:875 | (a) to be sentenced to imprisonment for life if he is guilty of an offence under paragraph 46(2)(a), (c) or (d);
-- src:876 | (b) to be sentenced to imprisonment for life if he is guilty of an offence under paragraph 46(2)(b) or (e) committed while a state of war exists between Canada and another country; or
-- src:877 | (c) to be sentenced to imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years if he is guilty of an offence under paragraph 46(2)(b) or (e) committed while no state of war exists between Canada and another country.
@ref Criminal Code s 47(2) (punishment for treason) (src:873-877)
`s 47(2)(a) the punishment of imprisonment for life` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for life`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 47(2)(c) (punishment for treason) (src:877)
`s 47(2)(c) the punishment of imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years` MEANS
    LIST Punishment OF `by indictment`, `imprisonment for a term of` `fourteen years`, `no imprisonment is stated`, `no fine is stated`, `no fine is stated`

@ref Criminal Code s 47(2) (punishment for treason) (src:873-877)
GIVEN act IS A `s 46(2) act`
      `a state of war exists between Canada and another country` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE (LIST OF Punishment)
`s 47(2) the punishment for treason` MEANS
    CONSIDER act
    WHEN `s 46(2)(a) uses force or violence for the purpose of overthrowing the government of Canada or a province` THEN JUST `s 47(2)(a) the punishment of imprisonment for life`
    WHEN `s 46(2)(b) communicates or makes available military or scientific information to an agent of a state other than Canada` THEN JUST (IF `a state of war exists between Canada and another country` THEN `s 47(2)(a) the punishment of imprisonment for life` ELSE `s 47(2)(c) the punishment of imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years`)
    WHEN `s 46(2)(c) conspires with any person to commit high treason or to do anything mentioned in paragraph (a)` THEN JUST `s 47(2)(a) the punishment of imprisonment for life`
    WHEN `s 46(2)(d) forms an intention to do high treason or anything mentioned in paragraph (a) and manifests that intention by an overt act` THEN JUST `s 47(2)(a) the punishment of imprisonment for life`
    WHEN `s 46(2)(e) conspires with any person to do anything mentioned in paragraph (b)` THEN JUST (IF `a state of war exists between Canada and another country` THEN `s 47(2)(a) the punishment of imprisonment for life` ELSE `s 47(2)(c) the punishment of imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years`)
    WHEN `s 46(2)(e) forms an intention to do anything mentioned in paragraph (b) and manifests that intention by an overt act` THEN JUST (IF `a state of war exists between Canada and another country` THEN `s 47(2)(a) the punishment of imprisonment for life` ELSE `s 47(2)(c) the punishment of imprisonment for a term not exceeding fourteen years`)
    WHEN `s 46(2) an act that is none of those in paragraphs (a) to (e)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): section 47(2) states a punishment only for an offence under paragraph 46(2)(a) to (e)

@ref Criminal Code s 47(2) (class of the offence of treason) (src:873)
`s 47(2) the class of the offence of treason` MEANS `an indictable offence`

-- src:878 | Corroboration
-- src:879 | (3) No person shall be convicted of high treason or treason on the evidence of only one witness, unless the evidence of that witness is corroborated in a material particular by evidence that implicates the accused.
@ref Criminal Code s 47(3) (corroboration) (src:878-879)
GIVEN `the offence charged is high treason or treason` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the conviction would rest on the evidence of only one witness` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that witness's evidence is corroborated in a material particular by evidence that implicates the accused` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(3) a conviction of high treason or treason on that evidence is barred` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the offence charged is high treason or treason` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "of high treason or treason"
        IF NOT `the conviction would rest on the evidence of only one witness` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "on the evidence of only one witness"
        IF `that witness's evidence is corroborated in a material particular by evidence that implicates the accused` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the evidence of that witness is corroborated in a material particular by evidence that implicates the accused"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- src:880 | Minimum punishment
-- src:881 | (4) For the purposes of Part XXIII, the sentence of imprisonment for life prescribed by subsection (1) is a minimum punishment.
@ref Criminal Code s 47(4) (minimum punishment) (src:880-881)
GIVEN `the question arises for the purposes of Part XXIII` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 47(4) the sentence of imprisonment for life prescribed by subsection 47(1) is a minimum punishment` MEANS
    IF `the question arises for the purposes of Part XXIII` THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "For the purposes of Part XXIII"

§ `Section 48 -- Limitation and information for treasonable words`

-- "more than three years after the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed": the third anniversary is inside the period (the Date constructor rolls 29 February forward to 1 March: fork F3).
-- src:882 | Limitation
-- src:883 | 48 (1) No proceedings for an offence of treason as defined by paragraph 46(2)(a) shall be commenced more than three years after the time when the offence is alleged to have been committed.
@ref Criminal Code s 48(1) (limitation) (src:882-883)
GIVEN `the proceedings are for treason as defined by paragraph 46(2)(a)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the offence is alleged to have been committed` IS A DATE
      `the date the proceedings were commenced` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(1) the proceedings are barred by the three-year limit` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are for treason as defined by paragraph 46(2)(a)` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "an offence of treason as defined by paragraph 46(2)(a)"
        IF Day `the date the proceedings were commenced` GREATER THAN Day `the third anniversary of the alleged offence` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "more than three years after" (a period fixed in the text's own words; not yet run)
    WHERE
        `the third anniversary of the alleged offence` MEANS
            Date (DATE_DAY `the date the offence is alleged to have been committed`) (DATE_MONTH `the date the offence is alleged to have been committed`) (DATE_YEAR `the date the offence is alleged to have been committed` PLUS 3)

-- (a) the information is laid "within six days after the time when the words are alleged to have been spoken"; (b) the warrant is issued "within ten days after the time when the information is laid".
-- Counted by calendar day, the last day included (fork F3): the clock times are not asked.
-- src:884 | Information for treasonable words
-- src:885 | (2) No proceedings shall be commenced under section 47 in respect of an overt act of treason expressed or declared by open and considered speech unless
-- src:886 | (a) an information setting out the overt act and the words by which it was expressed or declared is laid under oath before a justice within six days after the time when the words are alleged to have been spoken; and
-- src:887 | (b) a warrant for the arrest of the accused is issued within ten days after the time when the information is laid.
@ref Criminal Code s 48(2) (information for treasonable words) (src:884-887)
GIVEN `the proceedings are under section 47 in respect of an overt act of treason expressed or declared by open and considered speech` IS A BOOLEAN
      `an information setting out the overt act and the words was laid under oath before a justice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the words are alleged to have been spoken` IS A DATE
      `the date the information was laid` IS A DATE
      `a warrant for the arrest of the accused was issued` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the warrant was issued` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 48(2) the proceedings are barred unless the information and warrant came in time` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the proceedings are under section 47 in respect of an overt act of treason expressed or declared by open and considered speech` THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "in respect of an overt act of treason expressed or declared by open and considered speech"
        IF `paragraph (a) is met` AND `paragraph (b) is met` THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless (a) an information setting out the overt act and the words by which it was expressed or declared is laid under oath before a justice within six days ... and (b) a warrant for the arrest of the accused is issued within ten days"
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `paragraph (a) is met` MEANS
                `an information setting out the overt act and the words was laid under oath before a justice`
            AND Day `the date the information was laid` AT LEAST Day `the date the words are alleged to have been spoken`
            AND Day `the date the information was laid` AT MOST (Day `the date the words are alleged to have been spoken` PLUS 6)
        `paragraph (b) is met` MEANS
                `a warrant for the arrest of the accused was issued`
            AND Day `the date the warrant was issued` AT LEAST Day `the date the information was laid`
            AND Day `the date the warrant was issued` AT MOST (Day `the date the information was laid` PLUS 10)
